  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Complex Analysis - Derivatives Formula</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Find \(f'''(i)\) where \(f(z) = \frac{1}{z^2+{@k@}}\).</p>
<p>Answer: [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>We need to find the third derivative of \(f(z) = (z^2+{@k@})^{-1}\) at \(z=i\).</p>
<p>Using the chain rule:</p>
<p>\[ f'(z) = -1(z^2+{@k@})^{-2} \cdot (2z) = -2z(z^2+{@k@})^{-2} \]</p>
<p>\[ f''(z) = -2(z^2+{@k@})^{-2} - 2z(-2)(z^2+{@k@})^{-3}(2z) = -2(z^2+{@k@})^{-2} + 8z^2(z^2+{@k@})^{-3} \]</p>
<p>\[ f'''(z) = \dots \]</p>
<p>Evaluating at \(z=i\) (where \(z^2 = -1\)):</p>
<p>\[ f'''(i) = {@ta1@} \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber></idnumber>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025073100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>k:rand(4)+2;    /* k from 2 to 5, so z^2+k is non-zero at i */
fz: 1/(z^2+k);
d3fz: diff(fz, z, 3);
ta1: subst(z=%i, d3fz);
</text>
    </questionvariables>
