<!-- question: 169564 -->
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Complex Analysis - Contour Deformation Square</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Evaluate \(\oint_C \frac{1}{z^2+{@b@}z+{@c@}} dz\) where \(C\) is the square with vertices at \(\pm {@A@} \pm {@A@}i\).</p>
<p>Answer: [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>The denominator \(z^2+{@b@}z+{@c@}\) has roots at \(z = \frac{-{@b@} \pm \sqrt{ {@b^2-4*c@} }}{2}\).</p>
<p>For the given parameters, both roots lie inside the square \(C\).</p>
<p>Using the Residue Theorem (or partial fractions), the sum of the residues of \(f(z) = \frac{1}{(z-z_1)(z-z_2)}\) at \(z_1\) and \(z_2\) is:</p>
<p>\[ \text{Res}(f, z_1) + \text{Res}(f, z_2) = \frac{1}{z_1-z_2} + \frac{1}{z_2-z_1} = 0 \]</p>
<p>Thus, the integral is \(2\pi i \times 0 = 0\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber></idnumber>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025073100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>b:2;
c:2;  /* Roots are -1 +/- i */
A:3;  /* Square size 3, encloses roots */
ta1:0;
</text>
    </questionvariables>
