<!-- question: 169565 -->
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Complex Analysis - Maximum Modulus</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Find the maximum value of \(|z^2 + {@c@}|\) on the closed disk \(|z| \le {@R@}\).</p>
<p>Answer: [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>By the Maximum Modulus Principle, the maximum value of \(|f(z)|\) on a closed disk occurs on the boundary \(|z| = {@R@}\).</p>
<p>Let \(z = {@R@}e^{it}\). Then:</p>
<p>\[ |z^2 + {@c@}| = |{@R@}^2 e^{2it} + {@c@}| \]</p>
<p>This is maximized when \(e^{2it} = 1\) (since \({@c@} > 0\)), i.e., when \(z = \pm {@R@}\).</p>
<p>Max value = \({@R@}^2 + {@c@} = {@ta1@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
